  "title": "AI Tutor for MBA Students — Addressing Unmet Learning Needs in the US Higher Education Market",
  "executive_summary": {
    "title": "Executive Summary",
    "content": "This proposal outlines an AI Tutor for MBA Students in the United States, designed to provide personalized learning support. The broader US AI education market is projected for significant growth, potentially reaching $39.83 billion by 2035 [web-57da4247bdb54dd99b32029fe644c91b]. However, specific unmet learning needs, willingness to pay, and detailed product features for MBA students remain unconfirmed assumptions. Challenges include a relatively low perception of AI's benefits in education among the US public (39%) [web-236a31a2f5a04bcb8b4ae6d39dee9e37] and a notable adoption gap among higher education faculty, with only 22% regularly using generative AI compared to 83% of K-12 teachers [web-236a31a2f5a04bcb8b4ae6d39dee9e37]. The regulatory landscape for AI in education is rapidly evolving at both federal and state levels, with all 50 US states having introduced legislation on AI [web-57da4247bdb54dd99b32029fe644c91b, web-4bb0c35573164184b0269f72942c77e8]. The proposed business model is a direct-to-consumer subscription, with potential for institutional partnerships, but financial details are currently unsupplied assumptions.",
