    "title": "Target Customer",
    "content": "The primary target customer for the AI Tutor is MBA students in the United States. While there is a general familiarity with AI tools among students, with over half of US students aged 13-17 having used AI for research and ChatGPT leading student usage at 66% [web-57da4247bdb54dd99b32029fe644c91b, web-236a31a2f5a04bcb8b4ae6d39dee9e37], specific data for MBA students is lacking. A significant adoption barrier is the relatively low perception of AI's benefits in education within the US, where only 39% of respondents view it as beneficial [web-236a31a2f5a04bcb8b4ae6d39dee9e37]. Additionally, higher education faculty show a low adoption rate of generative AI (22%) compared to K-12 teachers (83%) [web-236a31a2f5a04bcb8b4ae6d39dee9e37], which could influence institutional acceptance and student trust. The precise unmet learning needs, frequency, urgency, and willingness to pay among MBA students for an AI tutor are currently unknown assumptions that require validation.",
